{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00446",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.22,
      "end_seconds": 5.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Afternoon, doctor. They're in and comfortable, and I have the measurements ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.64,
      "end_seconds": 8.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 9.78,
      "end_seconds": 15.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us. We came because of fever with chills."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.77,
      "end_seconds": 21.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "How long has this been going on? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.36,
      "end_seconds": 24.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "For one week, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.23,
      "end_seconds": 32.77,
      "duration_seconds": 7.54,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.1,
      "end_seconds": 56.49,
      "duration_seconds": 22.39,
      "text": "Um, it sort of comes and goes. I get some relief from paracetamol. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. There's a headache as well. And there's nausea as well, about a week now. With nausea, mild, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.92,
      "end_seconds": 60.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Let me know if I'm going too fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.22,
      "end_seconds": 63.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "No, you're fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.35,
      "end_seconds": 67.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Any stiff neck, rash, diarrhoea or breathlessness at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.77,
      "end_seconds": 73.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "I haven't had stiff neck, rash, diarrhoea or breathlessness, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.11,
      "end_seconds": 75.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Has there been any vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.7,
      "end_seconds": 78.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "No, no vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.48,
      "end_seconds": 81.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "I see. Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.73,
      "end_seconds": 84.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Hmm, no, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.44,
      "end_seconds": 100.37,
      "duration_seconds": 14.93,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.74,
      "end_seconds": 102.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.89,
      "end_seconds": 107.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.56,
      "end_seconds": 113.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "My mother has migraines. So, my father had a heart attack."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.46,
      "end_seconds": 116.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.15,
      "end_seconds": 120.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Yes, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.91,
      "end_seconds": 126.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.58,
      "end_seconds": 128.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Yeah, not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.79,
      "end_seconds": 132.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.77,
      "end_seconds": 133.54,
      "duration_seconds": 0.77,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.4,
      "end_seconds": 145.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.9,
      "end_seconds": 150.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "I take paracetamol, 650 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 151.63,
      "end_seconds": 159.11,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the paracetamol was 1300 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.31,
      "end_seconds": 164.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.66,
      "end_seconds": 173.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.91,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me. It's spironolactone, 25 milligrams, once a day for my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.46,
      "end_seconds": 177.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "So, how long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.87,
      "end_seconds": 184.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "For two months. I used to take diclofenac, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.48,
      "end_seconds": 191.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.82,
      "end_seconds": 206.11,
      "duration_seconds": 13.29,
      "text": "I have arthritis in my knees. I took the morning off to come in today. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. I've had heart failure, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.44,
      "end_seconds": 228.96,
      "duration_seconds": 21.52,
      "text": "Right. Okay, heart failure, that's already on your record. Good to know. Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.45,
      "end_seconds": 232.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 233.02,
      "end_seconds": 240.15,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pulse is 103 beats a minute, temperature 39.0. BP is 108 over 66, respiratory rate 16."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.27,
      "end_seconds": 244.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Thanks. Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.36,
      "end_seconds": 257.32,
      "duration_seconds": 11.96,
      "text": "Not at the moment, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.04,
      "end_seconds": 262.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Okay, let's do a quick examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.6,
      "end_seconds": 265.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.98,
      "end_seconds": 284.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Your spleen tip is just palpable under the ribs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.41,
      "end_seconds": 285.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.89,
      "end_seconds": 289.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Tell me if anything hurts as I press."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.52,
      "end_seconds": 310.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "No rash anywhere on your body that I can see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.77,
      "end_seconds": 325.01,
      "duration_seconds": 12.24,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.17,
      "end_seconds": 331.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.55,
      "end_seconds": 339.77,
      "duration_seconds": 7.22,
      "text": "Putting it all together, it fits best with malaria until proven otherwise. A viral illness is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 340.2,
      "end_seconds": 342.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.11,
      "end_seconds": 357.79,
      "duration_seconds": 13.68,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with malaria until proven otherwise do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had fever with chills for one week, and no rash or vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.63,
      "end_seconds": 359.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.09,
      "end_seconds": 370.87,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "I'm going to order a malaria test, for fever after travel. Let's get blood tests, for fever. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.43,
      "end_seconds": 374.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.18,
      "end_seconds": 399.08,
      "duration_seconds": 23.9,
      "text": "Let's get a dengue test, for fever. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. Let the lab know you travelled recently, that's important for the tests. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 400.34,
      "end_seconds": 401.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 402.75,
      "end_seconds": 413.54,
      "duration_seconds": 10.79,
      "text": "If you get confused, very drowsy, or the shaking returns, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. Please come and see me after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 414.05,
      "end_seconds": 417.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 419.12,
      "end_seconds": 424.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 425.91,
      "end_seconds": 430.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "So, I come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 431.5,
      "end_seconds": 436.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 437.55,
      "end_seconds": 439.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Nothing more from me, doctor, thanks."
    }
  ]
}